    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nI love the persistent toggle view that Mini Diff provides. However, a split view still provides clear syntax highlighting of both files, whereas this overlay does not.\n\nGiven that it's reasonable to assume that the reference text should always be the same filetype, I think it would be great for mini.diff to apply lsp & treesitter highlight groups to the reference text that gets inserted.",
